# Company & Product Context

When `cursor/company/` exists, read `cursor/company/README.md` before product, scope or prioritization work.

## Source of truth

| Topic | File |
| --- | --- |
| Company index | `cursor/company/README.md` |
| Product backlog | `cursor/company/future-work/README.md` |
| Story registry | `cursor/company/future-work/STORY-REGISTRY.md` |
| Area taxonomy | `cursor/company/future-work/AREA-TAXONOMY.md` |
| Story log (per area) | `cursor/company/future-work/<area>/STORY-LOG.md` |
| Documentation policy | `cursor/docs/documentation-governance.md` |
| Domain summary | `docs/domain.md` |

Add vision, MVP plan and commercial notes under `cursor/company/` as the product grows. When docs conflict on scope, follow the vision or plan named in `cursor/company/README.md`.

Do not invent backlog IDs. Promote `FW-*` to an execution story before implementing. If `cursor/company/` is missing, skip this rule and use `docs/` plus the active feature package.
